course: dictionary
lesson: 7497
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them, the context, show you which meaning the writer means. «She said sorry to the group, stayed in at break to make the missing part, and asked the teacher if they could hand in the finished poster late.» A finished poster here is a project you made, a big printed picture or notice.
explain: Look for clues. «Lost cats often hide close by, so checking neighbours' sheds, putting up posters, calling vets and calling at quiet times help.» Putting up tells you a poster is something you hang on a wall.
explain: The second meaning is a person. «The vet's poster about grapes and dogs is TRUE, and an expert in the right field is usually worth trusting.» Here a poster is someone who posts messages online, and the words TRUE and worth trusting tell you what kind of person to believe.
fact: A poster is a big printed picture or notice you hang on a wall.
fact: A poster can also be a person who posts messages online.
fact: Poster is a noun, and its plural is posters.
fact: Clues such as putting up, school project or online show you which meaning is right.
fact: Film posters, lost dog posters and election posters are all printed notices.
exercise: «For a school poster in Toronto, Liam is good at drawing and Ava at writing.» What is a poster here? | A bag for carrying books | *A big printed picture made for a school project | A letter sent by post | A person who posts messages online
exercise: In «Lost cats often hide close by, so checking neighbours' sheds, putting up posters, calling vets», which word tells you a poster is hung up? | *putting up | quiet | sheds | calling
exercise: What does poster mean in «The vet's poster about grapes and dogs is TRUE»? | A kind of cereal | A dog's collar | A big printed notice on a wall | *A person who posts messages online
test: «Before an election, candidates try to get noticed: adverts, catchy slogans, posters, signs on lawns.» What is a poster here? | A small coin | A fast runner | *A big printed notice | A person who posts online
test: What is the best way to check the meaning of a new word in a sentence? | Choose the longest meaning you can find | Look only at the first letter | *Swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense | Ignore the whole sentence and guess
exam: «She said sorry to the group, stayed in at break to make the missing part, and asked the teacher if they could hand in the finished poster late.» What does poster mean here? | A letter sent by post | *A big printed picture made for a school project | A bag for carrying books | A person who posts messages online
